  {
    "id": "bare_act_Consumer_Protection_Act_2019_txt_sec_2_2",
    "text": "[Consumer Protection Act 2019 - Section 2: Definitions]\nSection 2. Definitions.\nIn this Act, unless the context otherwise requires,—\n(1) \"applicant\" means a consumer who files a complaint before the Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission;\n(2) \"complainant\" means a consumer, or any voluntary consumer association registered under any law for the time being in force;\n(6) \"complaint\" means any allegation in writing made by a complainant for obtaining any relief provided by or under this Act;\n(7) \"consumer\" means any person who buys any goods for a consideration which has been paid or promised or partly paid and partly promised;\n(10) \"defective product\" means any product which has a manufacturing defect, deficiency in quality, or non-conformance to standards prescribed under law.",
